
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Yosemite National Park</title>
</head>

<body>

    <h1>Yosemite National Park</h1>

    <img src="https://wallpaperaccess.com/full/2558322.jpg"
         alt="Yosemite National Park">

    <h2>About Yosemite</h2>

    <p>
        Yosemite National Park is a beautiful national park in California.
        It is known for its mountains, waterfalls, forests, meadows,
        and giant sequoia trees.
    </p>

    <p>
        Yosemite was first protected in 1864 and became a national park
        in 1890. The park covers nearly 1,200 square miles and attracts
        visitors who enjoy hiking, camping, photography, and exploring nature.
    </p>

    <h2>Famous Places in Yosemite</h2>

    <h3>Half Dome</h3>

    <img src="https://wallpaperaccess.com/full/2286855.jpg"
         alt="Half Dome in Yosemite">

    <p>
        Half Dome is one of Yosemite's most recognizable landmarks.
        It is a huge granite formation that rises nearly 5,000 feet
        above Yosemite Valley.
    </p>

    <h3>Yosemite Falls</h3>

    <img src="https://travpedia.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Yosemite-National-Park_11zon.webp"
         alt="Yosemite Falls">

    <p>
        Yosemite Falls is one of the most famous waterfalls in the park.
        The entire waterfall drops about 2,425 feet.
    </p>

    <h3>El Capitan</h3>

    <img src="https://wallpaperaccess.com/full/1406532.jpg"
         alt="El Capitan in Yosemite">

    <p>
        El Capitan is a massive granite cliff in Yosemite Valley.
        It is especially well known for rock climbing.
    </p>

    <h2>Wildlife</h2>

    <p>
        Yosemite is home to many different animals. Visitors may see
        black bears, deer, coyotes, foxes, squirrels, and many types
        of birds.
    </p>

    <p>
        It is important to respect wildlife and keep a safe distance
        from animals.
    </p>

    <h2>Activities</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>Hiking</li>
        <li>Camping</li>
        <li>Photography</li>
        <li>Rock climbing</li>
        <li>Exploring trails</li>
        <li>Visiting giant sequoias</li>
        <li>Sightseeing</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why I Want to Visit</h2>

    <p>
        I would like to visit the park because of its beautiful scenery
        and peaceful natural places. I would like to see the mountains,
        waterfalls, forests, and giant sequoia trees in person.
    </p>

